# Results & Monitoring

## Types

- Standard Dockerfile / single-file Compose flows use **`AnalysisResult`** (and related single-job shapes).
- **Project** (ZIP / multi-file) outcomes use **`ProjectAnalysisResult`**.
- **Do not** gate project views behind the same **errors/warnings** type guards that only fit single-file analysis—project payloads are structured differently.

## Project UI

- Show **`per_file_results`**, **`service_mappings`**, **`project_summary`**, **`image_build_results`** when present.
- **Per-file** rows should feel like the standard analysis experience (issues, scores, file identity) within the project shell.
- **Image build** cards: show **image metadata** (name/tag/digest when available) and **logs** (or log summary + expand).

## Monitoring

- Surface **running**, **partial**, **unhealthy**, **exited**, **failed**, **stopping**, **stopped_by_user**, **cleanup_completed**, and **disconnected** (WS/client) states **clearly**—different copy, color, and icons; no ambiguous "active" for dead processes.
- If a container **exits before metrics** exist, show an explicit message (no empty chart pretending health).
- **Do not** label exited/failed/stopped containers as **"Live"** or imply continuous metrics when the process has stopped.
